    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Naegele's Rule for EDD calculation: Add 7 days to the first day of Last Menstrual Period (LMP) and add 9 calendar months.",
        "Positive signs of pregnancy (fetal heart beats, fetal movement felt by examiner, ultrasound confirmation) are definitive exam answers.",
        "Apgar score parameters (Appearance, Pulse, Grimace, Activity, Respiration) assessed at 1 and 5 minutes post-birth are frequently tested.",
        "Management of Postpartum Hemorrhage (PPH) and drugs like Oxytocin, Misoprostol, and Ergometrine are high-yield topic areas."
      ],
      "id": "qu1gv10"
    },
